      "The fastest way to begin is People Bingo: every player gets a card with squares like 'someone who has a younger brother' and walks around looking for matches. It sparks a quick conversation between every two kids, without pressure. Once the ice cracks, Who Am I? is a great next step, and Simon Says gets the group out of their chairs if you want more energy.",
      "Tip for teachers and leaders: don't start with a circle where 'everyone says something about themselves'. That only works for kids who are already confident. A structured game with clear rules gives every child a role instead of putting them on the spot.",
