      "At this age the best game is one you can explain in one sentence and demonstrate in one second. Simon Says and Freeze Dance suit ages 4-6 for exactly that reason: the rule is simple, there is movement and music, and kids understand at once what to do. Young children find it hard to wait their turn and to lose, so skip elimination and scoring. Whoever 'gets it wrong' in Freeze Dance does a funny move and jumps straight back in. Keep rounds to 5-7 minutes and move on before interest fades.",
