      "Every minute kids spend waiting with nothing to do is an invitation to chaos. That's why Simon Says, Freeze Dance and Fact or Fib?, where the whole group votes at once, work so well. It also helps to split into fixed teams with a name and a color, each with its own spot in the room. Then you don't have to reorganize between games, and the team rivalry keeps kids engaged even when it isn't their turn.",
