      "The secret to a good quiz is mixing difficulty levels. Easy questions everyone knows keep motivation up, and a hard one here and there creates real tension. Fact or Fib? is an easy way in, since you only have to guess whether a fact is true, so even young kids can win. In a mixed-age group, play in teams, so the older kids' knowledge and the younger kids' guesses combine.",
